{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2b414149-5b84-49ed-a448-6a8ab03645d3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Now I understand the bugs clearly:\n\n1. **`publish()`** — generates the date from UTC server time, ignoring `client_tz`. A post at 23:30 Buenos Aires time (UTC-3 → 02:30 UTC next day) gets tomorrow's date.\n2. **`display_date()`** — converts the stored date into the *viewer's* timezone, which can shift the calendar day despite the \"noon anchor\" trick (e.g., noon UTC → 21:00 UTC+9 is fine, but edge cases with DST or large offsets can still flip).\n3. **`feed()`** — sorts by `date` string, not by actual submission time, so posts with different author-local dates aren't ordered by when they were received.\n\nLet me fix all three:\nNow update the tests to cover the new behavior:\nAll 10 tests pass. Here's a summary of the three bugs and their fixes:\n\n### What was wrong in [journal.py](file:///tmp/h-YH11v2/journal.py)\n\n| Bug | Where | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Date derived from UTC** | `publish()` stamped `post[\"date\"]` using `now.astimezone(UTC)` — ignoring `client_tz` entirely | Date is now derived from `now.astimezone(ZoneInfo(client_tz))`, the author's wall-clock date. If the client already supplies a `\"date\"` key, it's preserved as-is. |\n| **Display converts to viewer TZ** | `display_date()` re-anchored the date at noon UTC and converted to the viewer's zone | `display_date()` now returns `post[\"date\"]` verbatim — no conversion, ever. |\n| **Feed sorted by date string** | `feed()` sorted by `(date, author)`, which doesn't reflect submission order when authors share a calendar date | Feed now sorts by `received_at` (a new UTC server timestamp), falling back to `date` for legacy posts. |\n\n### New tests added to [test_journal.py](file:///tmp/h-YH11v2/tests/test_journal.py)\n\n- **Late-night Buenos Aires / Tokyo** — 23:30 local posts see their own local date, not the UTC date\n- **Viewer TZ is irrelevant** — a reader in UTC, Tokyo, or Auckland sees the same author-local date\n- **Feed orders by submission time** — a Tokyo post at 14:30 UTC comes before a BA post at 02:30 UTC next day\n- **`received_at` is always UTC**\n- **Client-supplied date passthrough** — existing callers that send a date don't get it overwritten\n","duration_seconds":67.493045,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":13035,"output_tokens":3691,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":95224,"total_tokens":16726}}}
